Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:55:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 074/154] fix(devtools): refuse a devtools window on an Atrium
 chrome surface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Inspecting the sidebar, the palette or the notes pad segfaulted the browser.
AtriumChromeContext builds every chrome surface in the OTR System Profile, and
ThemeServiceFactory's ProfileSelections names WithRegular, WithGuest and
WithAshInternals - the System Profile falls through to kNone. So GetForProfile
returns null and the devtools bindings constructor calls AddObserver on it. Its
destructor calls RemoveObserver the same way, so teardown was a second crash.

  BrowserTestBase received signal: Segmentation fault: 11
  #4  DevToolsUIBindings::DevToolsUIBindings(content::WebContents*) + 636

Guarding that deref is not the fix, and trying it is what showed why: with
ThemeService handled, the next frame down was ContentSettingsManagerImpl reaching
for CookieSettings. The profile is missing a family of services, not one, so the
FRONTEND is refused for a surface instead of chasing them.

CDP attachment is deliberately untouched - it needs none of those services, and it
is how the surfaces are actually inspected. Verified: an eval scenario still reads
the palette's own DOM through remote debugging, 5 passed 0 failed.

Reachable, which is why it is a fix and not a note: the surfaces appear in the
target list chrome://inspect offers.

Mutation-proven, on the second attempt. Making the predicate return false failed to
compile on an unused variable, and the test then ran against a stale binary and
passed - so the gate itself is mutated instead: left logging without returning, the
test crashes.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc b/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
index d35e810848e29..b3ed0a6df11d1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
@@ -868,6 +868,16 @@ void DevToolsWindow::ToggleDevToolsWindow(
     const std::string& settings,
     DevToolsOpenedByAction toggled_by,
     const content::DevToolsManagerDelegate::DevToolsOptions& devtools_options) {
+  // Refuse a FRONTEND on one of Atrium's own chrome surfaces. They live
+  // in the OTR System Profile, which has no ThemeService and no CookieSettings, and
+  // the bindings dereference those in turn - it segfaulted twice over before this
+  // gate. CDP attachment is deliberately untouched: it needs none of those
+  // services, and remote debugging of the surfaces is how they are inspected.
+  if (atrium::AtriumIsChromeSurface(inspected_web_contents)) {
+    LOG(WARNING) << "Atrium: refusing a devtools window on a chrome surface; "
+                    "attach over CDP instead";
+    return;
+  }
   scoped_refptr<DevToolsAgentHost> agent(
       DevToolsAgentHost::GetOrCreateForTab(inspected_web_contents));
   DevToolsWindow* window = FindDevToolsWindow(agent.get());
